# the startup splash (TUI-DESIGN-2 §5): the first frame is splash frame 0 with the `step 0/–` sentinel; a key at ~100 ms
# cancels it — the next frame shows the character and no wordmark row; the smoke checks the wordmark was drawn before the
# key and never after it, zero clears (§8.2 splash.steps)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect step 0/
# raw mode on (Ink's post-commit effect writes ESC[?2004h): a key sent earlier is a cooked-mode byte the kernel echoes
expect \x1b\[\?2004h
sleep 0.1
send h
expect (?:›|>) h
sleep 0.3
send \x03
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
